==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}}. Adverb is by [[ellipsis]] from {{term||in the mean while}}, noun being conventionally written as one word after the adverb.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The time between two events

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# During the [[time]] (that something is happening).
# At the same time, but [[elsewhere]].

====Synonyms====
* (''during the time''):
* (''at the same time but elsewhere''): [[in the meantime]], [[meantime]], [[the while]]

